BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2nd Annual Hope in Motion 5K & 1K: A Celebration of Recovery
DTSTART:20260927T080000
DTEND:20260927T130000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:6a28bc0e7b0843f90618becf9f57c7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Peer Recovery Center of Addison County for the 2nd An
 nual Hope in Motion 5K & 1K\, a community celebration of recovery\, resili
 ence\, connection\, and hope! Hope in Motion brings together people in rec
 overy\, families\, friends\, community partners\, and supporters from acro
 ss Vermont to celebrate the message that recovery is possible and recovery
  benefits our entire community. Choose the family-friendly 1K or take on t
 he 5K. Whether you run\, walk\, volunteer\, cheer from the sidelines\, or 
 simply come out to celebrate\, everyone is welcome. This event is about mu
 ch more than crossing a finish line. Funds raised through Hope in Motion h
 elp the Peer Recovery Center of Addison County continue providing free rec
 overy supports throughout Addison County\, including recovery coaching\, m
 obile recovery coaching\, street outreach\, youth outreach\, emergency dep
 artment recovery coaching\, groups\, community outreach\, and other peer-b
 ased services. Our goal this year is to raise $40\,000 to help sustain cri
 tical recovery services\, including Mobile Recovery Coaching and Street Ou
 treach. Come move with us\, celebrate recovery\, reduce stigma\, and help 
 keep hope in motion throughout Addison County. All are welcome. You do not
  need to be in recovery to participate or support the event.\n\nSources: V
 ermont Public
LOCATION:Porter Hospital\, 55 Collins Dr
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/2nd-annual
 -hope-in-motion-5k-amp-1k-a-celebration-of-recovery-31-08-2026-18-47-46
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alex Radus and Stu Fuchs at Stage 33 Live
DTSTART:20260927T150000
DTEND:20260927T170000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:08a406dbbed0fe05e9068fe4b00fce@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Alex Radus puts songwriting at center stage\, pairing storytel
 ling and soulful vocals across an eclectic mix of Americana\, folk\, swing
 \, and blues. He learned from some of the nation’s best finger-pickers a
 t the Augusta Heritage Center\, which influenced his unique finger style a
 nd respect for traditional music. He's been direct support for John Gorka
 \, Richie Havens\, Darrell Scott\, Chris Barron (Spin Doctors)\, and more.
  He was a staple of NYC’s early aughts Anti-Folk scene at the Sidewalk C
 afé\, performing alongside Regina Spektor\, Nellie McKay\, and the Moldy 
 Peaches. More recently\, he was selected as a 2024 Falcon Ridge Folk Fest 
 Emerging Artist and voted a “Most Wanted” artist to return to the Main
  Stage in 2025. "A a remarkable artist... excellent guitarist\, songwriter
  and singer... moves across multiple genres with effortless virtuosity... 
 worth going out of your way to hear." — John Gorka Stu Fuchs is an award
  winning\, classically trained improvisational multi-instrumentalist blend
 ing mindfulness and music\, from bright and playful to relaxed and meditat
 ive. His concerts are like a combination of a summertime lawn bowling part
 y\, a mystical poetry reading in a Bedouin tent\, a smoky jazz club\, a nu
 anced recital hall concert\, and heart-opening meditation class. In additi
 on to being a ukulele minstrel\, Stu has toured to three continents perfor
 ming gypsy jazz guitar and meditative guitar styles with renowned sacred c
 hant artist Snatam Kaur. He recorded on her Grammy-nominated 2018 release 
 Beloved. "Respectfully pushes the Ukulele to brave new heights\, while kee
 ping one foot rooted in a number of time honored traditions." — Lil' Rev
 \, Author of the Hal Leonard Ukulele Method\, Entertainer & Music Historia
 n Alex Radus and Stu Fuchs split the bill in a 3:00 matinee on September 2
 7\, 2026. Tickets are $20 in advance through stage33live.com\, or at the d
 oor as available. Advance tickets guarantee entry. Only 40 tickets will be
  sold. All ticket proceeds go to the performers. The performances will be 
 recorded and filmed. Stage 33 Live is a casual and intimate industrial-rus
 tic listening room in a former factory hosting local\, regional\, and nati
 onal performances and presentations of original material. No bar or kitche
 n\, the stage is the mission\; coffee / soda / juice / water and weird sna
 cks available by donation. More information about the nonprofit\, all-volu
 nteer project\, and this and other upcoming events\, online at stage33live
 .com Stage 33 Live gratefully acknowledges the help of so many individuals
  without whom none of this would be able to happen\, and institutional sup
 port this season from The Island Corporation\, WOOL-FM\, Guilford Sound\, 
 and the Rockingham Arts & Museum Project to help fund improvements and mai
 ntenance\, and generally smooth out a lot of the rough edges. Stage 33 Liv
 e is a 501(c)3 nonprofit organization\, and all donations are deductible t
 o the fullest extent. Volunteers run the thing from stem to stern.\n\nSour
 ces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Stage 33 Live\, 33 Bridge Street\, Bellows Falls VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/alex-radus
 -and-stu-fuchs-at-stage-33-live-05-09-2026-11-07-47
END:VEVENT
