BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Concerts @ First: HairPeace
DTSTART:20260927T150000
DTEND:20260927T170000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:9e02659be19724dad5cf98215976e7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:HairPeace is a long-running acoustic folk-rock\, Americana and
  bluegrass vocal duo based in Indian River County\, Florida. Active togeth
 er since 1993\, they feature close vocal harmonies and a mix of original m
 usic and 1960s inspired covers. They have shared stages with national acts
  like The Little River Band\, Roseanne Cash\, and Asleep at the Wheel. Thi
 s promises to be a wonderful concert and we are delighted to be able to br
 ing these talented musicians to you\, all the way from their home base in 
 Florida. We hope you will join us!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:First Congregational Church of Essex Junction\, 39 Main St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/community-
 concerts-first-hairpeace-26-08-2026-07-10-14
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fairy House Festival
DTSTART:20260927T100000
DTEND:20260927T160000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:964ec98fd899dc23bd9590f0b1a3a2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Each September\, over 90 volunteers transform the woods around
  The Nature Museum into an enchanted village — tiny dwellings of bark\, 
 stone\, and moss tucked among the trees\, opening a portal to the living w
 orld all around us. Walk the forested trail\, build your own fairy house\,
  and spend the day enjoying live music\, bubbles\, crafts\, food\, local v
 endors\, and community. The Fairy House Festival is The Nature Museum's pr
 imary fundraiser and a beloved autumn tradition. Adults $18 ($20 at the ga
 te) Kids $5 Under 3 free\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Nature Museum\, 186 Townshend Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/fairy-hous
 e-festival-10-08-2026-08-18-20
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jackson Gillman\, the Stand Up Chameleon
DTSTART:20260927T130000
DTEND:20260927T150000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:f541ed0a21181b464ca16db1e14da2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Brookfield Old Town Hall as we bring you a fun
 \, family oriented afternoon with Jackson Gillman and his performance Awes
 ome Autumn. Jackson incorporates song\, story\, comedy\, dance\, mime and 
 sign language into his own intimate style of theatre. This heartwarming sh
 ow will celebrate the bounty and beauty of the season: Apples\, pumpkins\,
  cranberries\, a nip in the air\, flaming maples\, leaf piles\, migrating 
 geese…\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Brookfield Old Town Hall\, 93 Stone Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/jackson-gi
 llman-the-stand-up-chameleon-08-09-2026-12-46-33
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Long-running acoustic folk-rock duo HairPeace to Perform at First 
 Congregational Church of Essex Junction
DTSTART:20260927T150000
DTEND:20260927T163000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:13cbb3414969d4ac619d90cecffe30@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:HairPeace has been filling the air with music since 1993. Chry
 stine and Ray's close vocal harmonies blend the songs of the 60s and 70s w
 ith original material and an occasional modern tune\, bringing a sense of 
 peace\, love and community to every show. Joined by the incredible Kenny Z
  on upright bass\, this concert is a must-see! HairPeace has shared stages
  with national acts such as The Little River Band\, Roseanne Cash and Asle
 ep at the Wheel. You can visit their website (www.hairpeace.net) to listen
  to some of their music. This promises to be an amazing concert\, and we a
 re delighted to be able to bring these talented musicians to you\, all the
  way from their home base in Indian River County Florida. We hope you will
  join us! Tickets are available online at https://sevendaystickets.com/e/h
 airpeace or by calling the church office at (802) 878-5745. A portion of t
 he 2026 concert proceeds will support Age Well (www.agewellvt.org).\n\nSou
 rces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:First Congregational Church of Essex Junction\, 39 Main St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/long-runni
 ng-acoustic-folk-rock-duo-hairpeace-to-perform-at-first-congregational-chu
 rch-of-essex-junction-24-08-2026-12-55-50
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lynne Hanson at the Plainfield Opera House
DTSTART:20260927T160000
DTEND:20260927T180000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:290c8b539e2def5c06ef71d6674b39@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Come see two-time Canadian Folk Music Award winner Lynne Hanso
 n at the Plainfield Opera House! Lynne is an Ottawa-based\, Americana song
 writer known for her high energy roots guitar driven live performances wit
 h an authenticity that's as entertaining as it is disarming. A prolific so
 ngwriter\, Lynne has released ten studio albums along with two books of po
 etry over her 18 year solo career. She's toured extensively across North A
 merica\, Europe and the UK\, and appeared at leading international festiva
 ls including Take Root (Netherlands)\, Glasgow Americana (Scotland)\, Mave
 rick Festival (UK)\, Kerrville Folk Festival (US)\, and Winnipeg Folk Fest
 ival (Canada). She has also toured as support for Grammy-nominated artists
  like Gretchen Peters\, Steve Forbert and Albert Lee. Doors open at 3:30 p
 .m.\, concert at 4:00 p.m. All are welcome!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Plainfield Town Hall Opera House\, 18 High Street (Route 2)
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/lynne-hans
 on-at-the-plainfield-opera-house-25-08-2026-11-21-10
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music & Social Power w/ Dr. William Nash
DTSTART:20260927T140000
DTEND:20260927T160000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:929131519945c5bd149fa46a3ae5f8@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Middlebury College Professor William Nash for a multimedi
 a exploration of music and social power in American life as part of OCM's 
 fall festival\, Music in Troubled Times. Through recordings\, videos\, and
  historical images\, Nash examines how diverse musical traditions - from c
 ampaign songs and miners' songs to protest music - have reflected\, challe
 nged\, and shaped the nation's political and cultural history. Drawing on 
 his interdisciplinary expertise in American Studies and English\, Nash rev
 eals how music has long served as both a mirror of society and a force for
  change. This engaging lecture provides historical and cultural context fo
 r the festival's culminating production\, Rappahannock County. Town Hall T
 heater\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/music-soci
 al-power-w-dr-william-nash-15-09-2026-13-44-44
END:VEVENT
