BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WORDS OUT LOUD: Don’t Forget to Write\, reading by Vermont autho
 rs Ted Levin (nonfiction) and Emma Paris (poetry)
DTSTART:20260927T150000
DTEND:20260927T160000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:9c1a287820568050801c60fa7ac4d2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:WORDS OUT LOUD As part of event offerings for Art at the Kent
 ’s 2026 exhibit Throughlines at the Kents’ Corner State Historic Site
 \, WORDS OUT LOUD\, the popular Sunday afternoon fall reading series\, ret
 urns to the Old West Church. For this year’s final of three readings\, W
 ORDS OUT LOUD: Don’t Forget to Write\, welcomes Vermont authors Ted Levi
 n (nonfiction) and Emma Paris (poetry). To say “Don’t Forget to Write
 ” is to remind travelers to “stay in touch\,” to "send word" from af
 ar\, wherever they are. This year’s authors remember to write\, and they
  do so creatively and intelligently in prose and poetry. Readings will be 
 followed by receptions down the road at the Kent amidst the art on display
  for this year’s exhibit “Throughlines” where attendees may meet and
  chat with the authors and a selection of books will be available in the s
 hop. The WORDS OUT LOUD readings take place at the Old West Church at 3 o
 ’clock. Guests should arrive early to allow time for parking and seating
  at this historic 200-year-old meetinghouse in rural Calais\, bring layers
  for warmth\, and leave pets at home. Open to all. Donations welcome at th
 e door. With a few steps up into the vestibule\, the historic Old West Chu
 rch is not ADA accessible at this time. About the Writers September 27: Em
 ma Paris (she/her) served as the 2025 Vermont Youth Poet Laureate\, a posi
 tion awarded to the winner selected from a field of applicants\, all teen 
 writers (13–19)\, who submit a portfolio of their original poetry and CV
  info demonstrating their artistic excellence\, civic engagement\, and com
 munity impact. A junior at Bennington College\, where she studies Poetry a
 nd Environmental Science\, Emma was named an American Voices Nominee in th
 e 2023 Scholastic Art & Writing Awards\, is a 2025 Adroit Prizes Commended
  Writer\, and has been nominated for the 2026 Pushcart Prize. She has inte
 rned at both Green Writers Press and the Bennington Review\, working on th
 eir respective editorial staffs. Ted Levin is the author of\, most recentl
 y\, The Promise of Sunrise: Finding Solace in a Broken World as well as Ba
 cktracking: The Way of a Naturalist\, Blood Brook: A Naturalist’s Home G
 round\; Liquid Land: A Journey Through the Florida Everglades\, and other 
 works of nonfiction. A recipient in 2004 of the John Burroughs Medal\, awa
 rded annually to the author of a distinguished natural history book\, his 
 writing has appeared in Houghton Mifflin’s The Best American Sports Writ
 ing\, Audubon\, Sierra\, Sports Illustrated\, National Wildlife\, on Earth
 \, National Geographic Traveler\, National Geographic Books\, Yankee\, The
  New York Times\, Newsday\, The Boston Globe\, The Chicago Sun-Times\, The
  Guardian\, and The Daily Telegraph\, and elsewhere. For twenty-four years
 \, he was a regular commentator on Vermont Public Radio\, and occasionally
  on NPR. WORDS OUT LOUD 2026 has been organized by poet Mary Elder Jacobse
 n with the support of the Art at the Kent curatorial team.\n\nSources: Ver
 mont Public
LOCATION:Old West Church\, 758 Old West Church Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/words-out-
 loud-dont-forget-to-write-reading-by-vermont-authors-ted-levin-nonfiction-
 and-emma-paris-poetry-31-08-2026-14-50-25
END:VEVENT
