BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Philadelphia II Open Hours
DTSTART:20261012T100000
DTEND:20261012T120000
DTSTAMP:20260927T154133Z
UID:9c793bf684cd12918438e8acc510b6@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Soldiers in the Revolutionary War not only fought on boats\, t
 hey also often lived on them for months. Step aboard the Museum’s replic
 a of the Revolutionary War gunboat Philadelphia to explore their living an
 d working conditions\, understand the mechanics of the vessel\, and even r
 ow the oars! Aboard the vessel\, staff will have real artifacts from Revol
 utionary War sites around the lake (including recent artifacts recovered b
 y our archaeologists at Arnold’s Bay) for visitors to see\, touch\, and 
 learn about! Accessibility: The Philadelphia II is currently on the Museum
  Green. There is a staircase leading up to the boat\, and the boat is in t
 he middle of a grassy area. However\, the rigging and cannon from the Phil
 adelphia II are nearby or on the surrounding lawn\, and our staff would be
  happy to talk about the vessel as well as display props on the lawn. Staf
 f can also show artifacts on the lawn if needed. Lake Champlain Maritime M
 useum Every week through Oct 14\, 2026. Lake Champlain Maritime Museum 447
 2 Basin Harbor Road Vergennes \, Vermont 05491 802-475-2022 info@lcmm.org 
